      "question": {
        ":question/id": "c5c76511-c13a-59eb-bdbd-960c617d730f",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sin\\left(74^\\circ\\right)\\cot\\left(37^\\circ\\right)}{\\left(1+\\sin\\left(37^\\circ\\right)\\right)}\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Write $s=\\sin\\left(37^\\circ\\right)$ and $c=\\cos\\left(37^\\circ\\right)$. The **double-angle formula** gives $\\sin\\left(74^\\circ\\right)=2sc$.\n\n Also, $\\cot\\left(37^\\circ\\right)=\\frac{c}{s}$.\n\nRewrite the quotient ratio and cancel. Use $s^2+c^2=1$, factor the difference of squares, then cancel the matching binomial.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2sc\\frac{c}{s}}{(1+s)} &=\\frac{2c^2}{(1+s)} \\\\ &=2\\frac{1-s^2}{(1+s)} \\\\ &=2\\frac{(1-s)(1+s)}{(1+s)} \\\\ &=2(1-s) \\\\ &=2\\left(1-\\sin\\left(37^\\circ\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll cancellations use nonzero factors in the original expression.",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "709e0ce3-e957-51eb-923e-f80f3290c868",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
